The vector $\underset{\sim}{d}$ is shown on the grid.
Which column vector is $-5\underset{\sim}{d}$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-1,-4) grid (4,2);
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4) -- (0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (2,-3) node[midway,above right] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The vectors $\underset{\sim}{a}$ and $\underset{\sim}{b}$ are drawn on the grid.
Which statement is true?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-2,-1) grid (5,5);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (4,2) node[midway,below right] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\draw[->,thick] (1,4) -- (-1,3) node[midway,above] {$\underset{\sim}{b}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

